        "date_published": "2026-03-20T18:06:20+00:00",
        "description": "<p>Email is one of those tools we check daily but its underlying experience didn\u2019t evolve much. I use Gmail, as probably most of you reading this.<p>The Arc browser brought joy and taste to browsing the web. Cursor created a new UX with agents ready to work for you in a handy right panel.<p>I use these three tools every day. Since Arc was acquired by Atlassian, I\u2019ve been wondering: what if I built a new interface that applied Arc\u2019s UX to email rather than browser tabs, while making AI agents easily available to help manage emails, events, and files?<p>I built a frontend PoC to showcase the idea.<p>Try it: <a href=\"https://demo.define.app\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://demo.define.app</a><p>I\u2019m not sure about it though... Is it worth continuing to explore this idea?</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47458348\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47458348</a></p>\n<p>Points: 6</p>\n<p># Comments: 2</p>",
